  "body": "Implements the six accepted proposals from the cache-as-short-term-memory feasibility study (session brief: `CACHE-HAUNT_Proposals.md`, 2026-07-03). Cache-ghost doctrine gains two new hard laws grounded in real provider behavior.\n\n## The three hard laws (was one)\n1. **The seed stays dry** (unchanged) \u2014 the PNG is never the cache's hostage.\n2. **The cache is write-only** \u2014 real provider caches have no fetch API; warmth is only ever observed as `cache_read_input_tokens` on the *next* response. Warmth buys skipped prefill **compute** (~0.1\u00d7 price, big latency drop), never storage or bandwidth. `hydrate()` on a `write_only` substrate always rebuilds from the PNG.\n3. **The prefix is append-only** \u2014 providers match byte-exact prefixes. The old cache blob (`json.dumps(state, sort_keys=True)`) shifted early bytes every turn (`conversation` sorts first; `identity.updated_at` mutates), which would evict the whole entry on every wake. The cache-facing body is now one immutable genesis line + one appended line per turn; the selftest proves the byte-prefix property. PNG format untouched.\n\n## Changes\n- `src/mantle/ghost.py` \u2014 prefix-stable serialization (P2); `write_only`/`min_prefix_tokens` on `GhostSubstrate`; `TOO-SMALL-TO-HAUNT` gate (P5); per-wake warm/cold telemetry with nociception after 3 consecutive cold wakes (P4); `PREDICTED-WARM/COLD` status; heartbeat/TTL economics constants (P3); selftest grown 29 \u2192 48 checks.\n- `src/mantle/ghost_anthropic.py` \u2014 **new**: `AnthropicPromptCache`, a real write-only substrate over Anthropic prompt caching (P1). `warm`/`extend` map onto documented `max_tokens: 0` pre-warm requests with `cache_control` breakpoints laid out per the CACHE-HAUNT prefix law (P6). Lazy `anthropic` import, imported by nothing else \u2014 all gates stay keyless and offline.\n- `documents/Mantle_Reproduction.md` \u2014 the three-laws section + haunting governance (gate, telemetry, economics).\n- `README.md` \u2014 dependency-claim footnote for the one optional exception.\n\n## Gates (all green)\n`ghost selftest` 48/48 \u00b7 Stage-1 Zombie Body gate PASSED \u00b7 73/73 invariants \u00b7 a living spore (GHOST.png) re-warmed on the new code kept its cache slot and re-certified: verify 24/24, purity audit 52/0/0, VCW-conformant.\n\nNot yet exercised: `ghost_anthropic` against the live API (needs `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`; `python -m mantle.ghost_anthropic <spore.png>` performs one real warm and prints observed cache telemetry).\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)",
